    "application": "Actual current main/preload/production renderer, typed IPC, serialized LocalState and encrypted per-profile key storage. Fresh protected dummy profiles and hidden muted native windows. Shared provider Keychain adapters substituted to avoid personal entries. Non-fixture external requests blocked.",
    "before": "After actual required-key checks, hold enabled save before LocalState update. Remove actual OpenAI or ElevenLabs fixture key through typed IPC, then release save. Both original runs committed newsEnabled=true after key removal completed, without an alert. No provider requests.",
    "ordering": "17 variants hold actual key writers or enabled save at controlled checkpoints. For three providers, activation-first holds later deletion through temporary-file publication; deletion-first rejects activation; replacement-first uses the completed replacement. Further cases cover rejected-write queue recovery, keyless OFF bypass, sign-out, changed host/source/profile/availability and missing-key Resume. Two additional variants prove unselected X deletion/replacement does not become an RSS-profile prerequisite.",
    "prerequisites": "Nine rejected typed saves preserve all saved profiles. Positive controls accept RSS without X token and incomplete unavailable-profile OFF with no required keys.",
    "visibleJourneys": "Real UI removes both required keys during held activation. Both removals remain visibly pending until durable save, then missing-setup guidance appears and Turn off succeeds. Fresh default setup directly routes to sources, DJs, provider keys and mood with draft/focus retained; incomplete OFF save succeeds without keys.",
    "cadence": "Actual automatic text/voice run finishes while a second setup save waits behind a preceding enabled save in the credential queue. The second save captured running request identity before queue entry. It commits six-hour cadence anchored to the original run start and records the completed clip once.",
    "resume": "Two actual scheduler/service/native UI cases preserve failure/interruption through repair and ordinary Save, suppress implicit retry and dispatch once on separate Resume. Controlled no-story response makes no voice request, changes no selected take and leaves music paused.",
    "providers": "Activation and prerequisite cases make zero provider requests. Cadence and Resume use substituted OpenAI/ElevenLabs responses with actual service parsing/cancellation/storage; cadence returns valid saved MP3. No live or billed provider requests.",
    "checkpoints": "Test-only holds expose existing key-write and atomic rename boundaries. Scheduler reference invokes actual tick; production scheduler logic is retained. Activation-only scheduler timers are stopped to isolate save behavior."
  },
